From 82f1a018b3e8f87b2e51e8b447656e80d1d0589a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Troy Sargent <0xalpharush@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:20:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(certify): scoped stage proofs cut block by block

certify.py --cut proves every stage through cut points even without
loops; with --joins the MIR->schedule stage is cut at every block the
schedule map relates, and EVM IR segments are bounded by --segment.
With --exclude the proofs are about the calls whose selector is none
of the excluded ones: every segment assumes it, cut candidates only
come from code such a call reaches (the dispatcher's excluded cases,
excluded functions and their callees are pruned), and Stages composes
under that scope.

A cut is kept only where both programs end their segments together:
EVM IR join cuts need the same entry blocks on both sides, MIR->sched
block cuts need the scheduled stack (and each caller's words below a
call) to hold every live value, and MIR->MIR cuts inside a callee need
the callers to read the same values after the call. --no-mir-joins
keeps the MIR passes' stages whole.
